   "title": "Stage 1",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Stage 1 · Transcribe & edit the score\n\n1. Pick the recording in **Load Audio** (press R after adding files to Downloads).\n2. **Transcribe Recording** → SheetSage2. If the singer ends up in the instrument track, tick **isolate_vocals_first** (Demucs separates the singer, then SheetSage2 hears a vocal-forward mix) and re-run; the summary also tells you how many seconds of singing the recording has — an instrumental version shows 0, or un-mute **Fix Voices** (Ctrl+M) and pick a repair mode.\n3. **Score Editor**: on the first run its box fills with the score. Edit it right there (notes, chords, tempo `Q:`, section comments), then queue again: transcription is cached, only the editor and what follows re-run. Type `RESET` to reload the incoming score.\n4. The editor saves the score to `output/yue2_studio/edited_score.abc`. That file is what **Stage 2** loads, so you can also edit it in any text editor.\n\nRead **Score Facts** for tempo, key and sung notes per section before writing lyrics."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
